---
servings: 2
title: Precooked Breakfast Sausage (CSO)
tags: CSO, steam, AI
source.author: AI Search
course: Breakfast
prep time: 5 min
cook time: 10 min
description: Easily brown your pre-cooked breakfast sausage links or patties with no flipping, no greasy stove, and no standing over the hot stove.
---

Position the modular rack near the middle position of the #Convection Steam Oven{} (CSO). Place the solid sheet pan in the lower tray of the modular rack (optionally line with parchment paper for easy clean-up).
Preheat the oven to 375°F on Convection Steam mode.

Place the frozen or thawed @Breakfast Sausages{10}(pre-cooked, brown-and-serve) on the #perforated pan{} with spacing between the pieces.

> Use the perforated pan to allow air flow around and through the food for even browning. The solid pan underneath will catch any grease drippings.

After the oven has preheated, place the perforated pan on top of the modular rack. 

Cook for ~{6-8%minutes} if thawed, or ~{8-10%minutes} if frozen. Extend the cooking time if needed for your desired level of browning. Check that the sausages reach a safe internal temperature of 165°F.
